// A hexadecimal literal takes no suffix. At `0xFFi` the longest match is the
// INT `0xFF`, because `i` is not a hexadecimal digit, and `i` is a name, so the
// program has a name directly after a literal, a syntax error
// (spec/01-lexical.md, row `suffix-boundary`). A scanner that reads an optional
// `i` after each literal accepts it.
//
// A static error rejects the program: a non-zero exit status, and nothing
// runs, so nothing prints (spec/README.md, Conformance). The first line
// prints `ran`, so an implementation that finds the error only when it runs
// the program prints `ran` and fails this probe.

print "ran";
print 0xFFi;

// STATIC-ERROR
// STATUS: error
// COVERS: literal suffix-boundary
